    "ix.1": "The Town Square Problem — Meeting a Community’s Needs",
    "ix.2": "A Problem-Based Learning unit. Students step into a growing town, take on a stakeholder’s point of view, and solve a real, messy question — building from surface to deep to transfer learning. The teacher is a guide, not the answer key.",
    "ix.3": "<b>Driving question:</b> Miller’s Creek is growing. One empty lot on the town square is left — and families, shop owners, and town leaders all want something different for it. There isn’t enough money or space for everything. What should the community do?",
    "ix.4": "The three-phase path (do them in order)",
    "ix.5": "Problem-solving is a <b>transfer</b> move — it only works once students have knowledge to reason with. So the problem in Phase 3 is deliberately <b>gated</b> behind Phases 1 and 2.",
