    "ix.12": "⛔ <b>Gate:</b> don’t open the Phase 3 problem until students have finished the surface and deep activities. Meeting the problem too early turns inquiry into guessing.",
    "ix.13": "Big idea & objectives",
    "ix.14": "<b>Big idea:</b> Communities form to meet shared needs. Because resources are <b>scarce</b>, people must weigh options and decide together — that is the heart of good citizenship.",
    "ix.15": "<b>Know:</b> why people form communities, how communities meet needs, and what scarcity, supply, and demand mean.",
    "ix.16": "<b>Understand:</b> the same empty lot looks different from each stakeholder’s point of view.",
    "ix.17": "<b>Do:</b> run the problem-solving process end to end — name a problem, gather information, weigh options, choose a solution, and check it (§113.14(c)(16)(B)).",
    "ix.18": "Standards this unit is aligned to (§113.14)",
